  m_text: "<b>The Aravali Hills</b> form one of the oldest fold mountain ranges in
    the world, stretching northeast\u2013southwest across Rajasthan. They act as
    a natural barrier, preventing the desert from expanding eastward. Composed mainly
    of ancient rocks, the Aravalis are low in height but rich in minerals and biodiversity.
    Mount Abu, the highest peak, also has evergreen forest patches that contrast
    sharply with the nearby desert."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
