  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: <b>The Luni River </b>is the only major river flowing through the Thar
    Desert. Originating in the Aravali Hills near Pushkar, it flows southwest and
    disappears into the Rann of Kutch due to high evaporation. Its water is saline,
    especially in the lower reaches, making it unsuitable for drinking, but useful
    for irrigation near its upper course. The Luni symbolizes the temporary and fragile
    nature of desert rivers, active only during brief monsoon showers.
